		<profileDesc>
			<abstract>
				<p>We use pairings over elliptic curves to give a collusionresistant traitor tracing scheme where the sizes of public keys, secret keys, and ciphertexts are independent of the number of users. Prior constructions from pairings had size Ω(N 1/3). An additional consequence of our techniques is general result showing that attribute-based encryption for circuits generically implies optimal traitor tracing.</p>
			</abstract>
